C 0x51A9 0xE071 goes up: no other prize is accepted on this stage
L 0x51AE compare_hyper
C 0x51AE HYPER
L 0x51B1 compare_word   Compares what was typed in 0xE1E8 with the word at DE; 0x0D ends it, and it exits without carry if it matches
C 0x51B5 The 0x0D separates one word from the next
C 0x51BD Carry set: no match
D 0x51BF 0x5243 texts  Strings separated by 0x0D: HYPER, BAKA, AHO, LASER, MISSILE, SHIELD, OPTION, DOUBLE, DOWN, and then the names that come by default in the high score table: MOMOKO, CHIE, AKEMI, SYUKO, CHIAKI, NORIKO, SATOE, YASUKO, KINUYO, HISAE, MIYUKI, YOHKO.
F 0x51BF 16
L 0x5243 which_key_is_pressed   Walks the eight keyboard rows with SNSMAT and returns the character of the first key pressed
C 0x5248 SNSMAT: keyboard row E
C 0x524B A cpl: on the keyboard a pressed key is a zero
C 0x5250 Eight rows
C 0x5253 With nothing pressed, 0xE1E1 to zero
C 0x5259 The row times eight: eight keys per row
C 0x5263 It looks for the set bit, which is the key
